Erik Kleinbussink <Erik.Kleinbussink@lmco.com> wrote:
: I am looking for a utility which allows X windows to be redirected
: across gateway machines. In other words, my display is at least two
: telnet's away from the machine I am working on.

: On AIX3.2 I had the binary to a neat utility called xrelay, which
: when run on an intermediary machine, read incoming X traffic as if it
: were server:0 or server:1 and then forwarded the X traffic onto the
: next piece of its journey.

: This allowed me to use X applications on non-local machines.

Why don't you redirect the x app to the original site?

[site x]----telnet--->[site y]--telnet-->[site z]--telnet-->[site k]

on site x issue command xhost +site k (if it is a unix machine). On site k
start the x application like:
%xapplicatin -display site x:0.0
it will redirect the display to site x.

Mihaly



