Brian --

perhaps someone can provide you with a more precise answer, but my initial
suggestion would be to check the server-pool regulation in NS's config. If
I recall correctly (using Apache now), you should be able to set not only
the max/min number of idle server instances, but also the number of
clients served by one of these before they're killed off.

this functionality exists for a reason, namely taking care of screwy
servers. Try scaling back whatever you have these values set to presently
and see if your problem goes away. 

I will typically set max clients per child to ~30. The server pool sizes
obviously depends on your situation (though siting that 4100, I'd imagine
you keep it relatively high)..

..kg..
kevin graham

