: Greetings!
: The graphics card is some model of ZLXp; the manual says ZLXp-E1 or 
: ZLXp-E2, but I don't know which of the two the card is. I don't have the 
: manual in front of me, and the stuff I've been finding on the web makes me 
: believe my memory may be faulty.

: The problem is that the card works great in console mode, but once X starts
: up the monitor complains that the scan rate is out of range. Searching the 
: web, I find references to setting the card's scan rate using DIP switches 
: on the module. The card these folks have doesn't have dip switches; just a 
: single jumper to enable some sort of VGA compatibility mode and a jack for 
: 3D goggles. Since I have no DIP switches, I'm starting to think I've 
: misremembered what the manual said the card was.

: Is there some place on the web where specs on Digital monitors (scan rates
: they like, etc.) and video cards (the scan rates OSF/1's X server likes to
: use, etc.) are listed?

: Is there some way other than the mythical DIP switches to control the scan
: rate being used by the X server? Man Xdec isn't terribly helpful; the only
: relevant option seems to be "-screen n" with a pretty vague description of
: how to specify n.

I copy to articles from this group here, maybe it will help you.

Mihaly
-----------------------------------
> Is there a way to change the Xserver resolution in Digital UNIX 4.0x or
> tune the refresh rates?
>
> So far, I haven't been able to find information in the documentation.
>
>

Add command line options to the Xdec command line.  The typicalplace is in
/usr/var/X11/Xserver.conf, the canonical location of the
server configuration file on DU.  Options:

        -screen[<num>] <width>[x<height>]
        -vsync[<num>] <rate>
        -I -e3stereo[<num>] <rate>

Where:

        <num>        Screen number starting from 0
        <width>      Width in pixels
        <height>     Height in pixels
        <rate>       Refresh rate in Hz

-screen and -vsync must be before any -I option and -e3stereo
applies only to 4D40T-4D60T cards.  Examples:

        -screen0 1920x1280
        -vsync 75 -screen 1280


--
Monty Brandenberg                                      Consulting for:
MCB, Inc.                                              Digital Equipment
Corp.
45 Putnam Avenue           mcbinc@world.std.com
montyb@eng.pko.dec.com
Cambridge, MA 02139        617.864.6907                508.493.2702

-------------------------
You'll find the information I think you are looking for in the Digital UNIX
4.0b release notes section 3.3.2 page 3-3.
for X11 it requires editing  /usr/lib/X11/xdm/Xservers and changing
":0 local /usr/bin/X11/X -nice2" to
":0 local /usr/bin/X11/X -nice2 -screen 0 800"

for CDE it requires editing /usr/dt/config/Xservers and Xservers.con
":0 Local local@console /usr/bin/X11/X :0 -nice2" to
":0 Local local@console /usr/bin/X11/X :0 -nice2 -screen0 800"

make sure your screen supports 800x600 before you do this.  
Hope it Works for you.



