On Wed, 21 Jan 1998 17:06:10 -0500, Dan <dkirkpatrick@hotmail.com>
wrote:

>We're running Digital Unix v3.2c with the bundled Sendmail...
>
>How do I go about getting a POP service installed so we can use POP to
>grab mail off the unix box to PC's???

First create a user called pop and a group called pop to which the
user po must belong. Create a directory called /usr/spool/pop owned by
pop. Create a file called POP in this directory with entries in it of
the form:

  :user code::usercode:::::::0i

for each user.
use the program /usr/lib/mh/popwrd to assign a password to each pop3
user set up in the /usr/spool/pop/POP file. Use /usr/lib/mh/popaka to
create a list of aliases for inclusion in /var/adm/sendmail/aliases
(you'll need to run newaliases after editing this file).

The final bits are to ensure that the permissions on /usr/lib/mh/spop
are:
  -rwsr-xr-x   

and to run the popd daemon using:

  /usr/lib/mh/popd -p 110 > /dev/null 2>&1 &


Hope this helps.



