Last week I attached a DCAS-34330 to an Alphastation 255 running 
Digital Unix 4.0B and there was no problem at all. 
It was on SCSI adapter 0 and had I gave it a target SCSI ID of 5,
so all I had to do was

  # cd /dev
  # ./MAKEDEV rz5
  # disklabel -rwn rz5 DCAS-34330

and create the filesystem on it (or whatever).
There is no need for an appropriate disktab entry, the OS queries
the disk for the appropriate geometry information.

I assume by dec osf 1.3 you mean OSF/1 v3.something.
My guess is that this will behave the same as 4.0B, but can't say
for sure.  Anyone?

Mark

