I was having very frequent failures (10-50%) during address resolution
with the current communicator beta running on 4.0a.  The system was
also running with significant paging load due to the *cough* feature-richness
of NSC.  Upping physical memory from 64M to 96M helped the paging and
more surprisingly, greatly reduced connection failures.  The only explanation
I have is that a timer is running and sometimes causing EINTR returns
on some calls that aren't being handled correctly.  The slower NSC runs,
due to paging, say, the more likely this is to happen.

