> based on the values.  E.g. for enum bool {TRUE, FALSE} the
> compiler could choose char and only allocate a byte.  But
> for enum x {y = 1<<22}, the compiler must choose a type
> large enough to hold 1<<22, unless 1<<22 is not a value
