From what I have heard, /etc/disktab is not used for SCSI disks under
Digital Unix 4.x. The Jaz drive is not well-behaved enough to get the
drive geometry from the drive itself, so you get this kind of error.

There are a couple of possible workarounds. If you have access to a 3.x
system, create an appropriate disktab entry and use disklabel.

Otherwise, you need to get a disk label from someone who has a good Jaz
cartridge, put it in file, and copy it (probably using dd) to the raw
disk. There was a package, written by kevin.s.partin@boeing.com, which
was posted a while back, which will do all this and more. e-mail me if
you would like a copy.
-- 
	- Jay Olson (jjo@triton.com)
