Guy Finney wrote:
> 
> I thought this would be easy, but apparently I was wrong.  I'm trying to add
> an external JAZ drive to my au433 running 4.0c. It's SCSI ID is 3.
> 
> Apparently 'disklabel' doesn't approve of it, or else I'm misunderstanding
> something (hopefully the latter).  The command:
>         disklabel -wrn rz19 jaz
> gives the error "jaz: unknown disk type". I don't know where it came up with
> rz19, but that's what I found when I rebooted after making the connection.
> 
> Any advice or insight would be appreciated.
> 
> --
> Guy Finney
> gaf@primenet.com

You get rz19 because your drive is on SCSI bus 2: 19 = 2*8 + 3.
For disklabel to recognize "jaz" you must have an entry in /etc/disktab
that gives information about the JAZ drive - size, partitions, etc.

Marian Szebenyi
MacCHESS, Cornell U.



