Michael Waite wrote:
> 
> I Have Digital Unix 4.0b and an external modem.  I have tip connecting
> to my ISP. The PPP garbage scrolls across the screen.  What do I need to
> do (configure) to be able to browse the Internet with Netscape?
> 
> I have a small local tcpip network here at my house (three machines)
> How will this be affected by my configuration of dial out access.
> Ideally I want to use my DEC Alpha to be the gateway for the other two
> nachines.
> 

Check the following man pages:
ppp_manual_setup (7)    - Describes how to manually set up 
			  Point-to-Point Protocol (PPP) connections
pppd (8)                - Point-to-Point Protocol (PPP) daemon
pppstats (8)            - Print Point-to-Point Protocol (PPP) 
			  statistics
startppp (8)            - Starts the pppd daemon for PPP dial-in 
			  connections

After you are connected, make sure that the default route in your
Alpha points to your ISP and that the default routes in your other
machines point to the Alpha. You will of course have already made
arrangements with your ISP for DNS etc.

Charlie


