Jean-Pierre Sauthier wrote:
> 
> I bought a new Seagate 19171N 9GB HD and want to label it under Digital
> Unix V3.2G
> Where can I find the needed Info ? i.e. default partition size, type, heads
> etc.
> Thanks for help !
> Jean-Pierre Sauthier

Let the operating system and the disk sort it out! Do something like

disklabel -wr rz0 xyz

(where you should replace the rz0 with the correct disk of course).
This forces D.U. to interrogate the disk and returns a sensible 
set of partitions (which you may wish to then edit).
