Organization: Erol's Internet Services
Newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1


Your sysconfigtab looks pretty reasonable to me.

Have you checked your files for fragmentation? You especially want to
make sure your BMT isn't fragmented. 

	showfile -e <mount-point>/.tags/-6

will display the number of extents in the BMT. I always try to make
the BMT big enough that it never gets extended.

You may also want to get a kernel profile and see where your system is
spending its time. I would recommend using DCPI rather than kprofile
for that.

